{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicConformElectrolytes",
    "description": "MOSAIC's conform_electrolytes(jtotal): SUBROUTINE conform_electrolytes of chem/module_mosaic_therm.F (WRF v4.8.0) with calculate_xt, the form_* salt formers, degas_hno3 / degas_hcl / degas_nh3 and electrolytes_to_ions. It turns a bin's total species amounts, as the host hands them to MOSAIC, into a set of electrolytes that is chemically consistent, sends the volatile acids and ammonia nothing can hold back to the gas, and recomputes the species from the electrolytes. mosaic_dynamic_solver calls it on every bin before ASTEM, and ASTEM_non_volatiles calls it again after H2SO4/MSA condensation; ions_to_electrolytes.esm is the LIQUID-phase counterpart that MESA calls.\n\nTHE RULE is a fixed ORDER of salt formation, each salt taking as much of its two ions as the scarcer allows (min of the two, scaled by stoichiometry), the remainders passed on. It is written here as that chain of remainders: an algebraic sequence of assignments, not an iteration (nothing is solved; every quantity is a closed-form function of the ones before it).\n\nDOMAIN: X_T (template aerosol_xt) of the clipped bin; X_T >= 1.9999 (binary32, mp.xt_split_i2e) or X_T < 0 is sulfate-POOR, otherwise sulfate-RICH. Both start with CaSO4 = min(Ca, SO4) and Ca(MSA)2 = min(Ca, MSA/2).\n\nSULFATE-POOR, in order: Na2SO4, NaMSA, Ca(NO3)2, NaNO3, then ALL remaining sodium as NaCl -- if chloride runs short the deficit is taken from gas-phase HCl, and if that runs out too the chlorine is created (hcl_created; form_nacl books it in total_species and tot_cl_in) -- then CaCl2, ALL remaining calcium as CaCO3 (carbonate is set to it), (NH4)2SO4, NH4MSA, NH4NO3, NH4Cl, free MSA. Nitrate, chloride and ammonium left over are degassed. Sulfate left over after (NH4)2SO4 is discarded (so4_lost; FORTRAN_BUGS B33): it exists only for 1.9999 <= X_T < 2.\n\nSULFATE-RICH: NaMSA, NH4MSA, free MSA, then the sulfate by the cations left per sulfate, xt_prime = (Na + NH4)/SO4, against xna_prime = 1 + (Na/2)/SO4: regime 1 (xt_prime >= xna_prime) Na2SO4 and then (NH4)2SO4 + letovicite (NH4/SO4 >= 1.5) or letovicite + NH4HSO4; regime 2 (xt_prime >= 1) NH4HSO4 then Na2SO4 + NaHSO4; regime 3 NaHSO4, NH4HSO4 and H2SO4. Without sulfate after CaSO4 (regime 0) nothing more forms. Every nitrate and chloride is degassed, and the ammonium left (none in regime 1, whose letovicite step zeroes the store) too. Calcium left after Ca(MSA)2 would be discarded, but that needs X_T > 2 and so is never reached here.\n\nOUTPUT: the electrolytes elec (in the `el` order of mosaic_thermo_parameters), the species a = sum over electrolytes of elec * tp.stoich * mp.ion_species (electrolytes_to_ions, which therefore never returns a discarded remainder), carbonate co3, the amounts degassed, and the gases g. The Fortran's summation order in electrolytes_to_ions differs from the stoichiometric sum's; every term is non-negative, so the two agree to a few ulps.\n\nGASES ACROSS BINS: mosaic_dynamic_solver conforms bin 1, 2, ... in turn on one gas vector, so a bin's HCl clamp sees what the bins before it degassed. The component takes the gases per bin (g_in[lev, bin, gas]); a consumer that runs all bins at once must hand bin b the g of bin b-1 (a genuine sequential dependence along `bin`, through the HCl clip alone; HNO3 and NH3 only accumulate).\n\nPRECISION: double precision throughout; 1.9999 and the 1.e-15 guard (so4_tiny) are binary32 literals, the 0.5, 2, 3, 1.5 exact.\n\nTESTS: WRF's own compiled conform_electrolytes (main/libwrflib.a of the B30-fixed chem170 build) run by kernels/mosaic_conform_driver (WRF fork, branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, 88c6f446) on (i) the bins mosaic_dynamic_solver conforms at model steps 364 and 1026 of the chem170 MOSAIC capture (dumps/chem170_full_mosaic: aer(:, jtotal) = rsub0 * conv1a by map_mosaic_species, the gases carried bin to bin as the solver does), a selection covering every branch the column takes, and (ii) hand-specified bins for the branches the column never reaches (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/conform64). Real64 at rel 1e-9 with an absolute floor of 1e-12 of the bin's largest amount; the domain and regime flags are pinned (rel 0).\n\nCELL AXES: every quantity carries the cell axes [lev, bin] (metaparameters NLEV and NBIN, 1 by default) ahead of its own, as in ions_to_electrolytes.esm; elementwise relations are written on bare names, and only the gathers and the stoichiometric sum name the cell subscripts.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Fast, J.D., Peters, L.K. (2008). Model for Simulating Aerosol Interactions and Chemistry (MOSAIC). J. Geophys. Res. 113, D13204."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F"
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "Grid cells (model levels) evaluated at once; 1 for a single cell. Bound by a column coupling."
    },
    "NBIN": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "MOSAIC size sections per cell (nbin_a); 1 for a single bin. Bound by the coupling that mounts this component (8 in chem_opt = 170)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NLEV"
    },
    "bin": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NBIN"
    },
    "sp": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 7
    },
    "el": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 22
    },
    "ion": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 9
    },
    "gas": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 5
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicConformElectrolytes": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "tp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm"
        },
        "mp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_mesa_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "a_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "bin",
            "sp"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The bin's TOTAL species amounts aer(:, jtotal) on entry to conform_electrolytes, in the `sp` order so4, no3, cl, nh4, msa, na, ca (aer indices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 108, 109), nmol per m3 of air. Negative values are clipped to zero first, as the Fortran does in place. (The routine overwrites aer(ico3_a) without reading it, so carbonate is not an input.)"
        },
        "g_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "bin",
            "gas"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "The gas amounts this bin's call sees, in the `gas` order H2SO4, HNO3, HCl, NH3, MSA (nmol/m3); only HNO3, HCl and NH3 are touched. mosaic_dynamic_solver conforms the bins one after another, so bin b sees what bin b-1 degassed: a consumer hands each bin the gases the previous one left."
        },
        "so4_tiny": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 1.0000000036274937e-15,
          "description": "form_lvcite_nh4hso4's guard: NH4/SO4 is formed only above store(iso4_a) > 1.e-15, a default-REAL literal (binary32 1.0000000036274937e-15)."
        },
        "so4_0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "shape": [
